    "markdown": "---\ntitle: search\n---\n\n\n\n```python\nsearch(text, dataset=None, ref=None)\n```\n\nFind variables whose name, label or description contain every word of ``text``.\n\nMatching ignores case and accents (``\"educacion\"`` finds \"Educación\"). Results\nare ranked: matches in the variable name or label come first.\n\n## Parameters {.doc-section .doc-section-parameters}\n\n| Name    | Type        | Description                                                 | Default    |\n|---------|-------------|-------------------------------------------------------------|------------|\n| text    | str         | One or more words, e.g. ``\"poverty\"`` or ``\"night lights\"`` | _required_ |\n| dataset | str \\| None | Search only this dataset                                    | `None`     |\n\n## Returns {.doc-section .doc-section-returns}\n\n| Name   | Type             | Description                                                                                                                                                                                                                          |\n|--------|------------------|--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n|        | pandas.DataFrame | One row per variable and scale: ``dataset``, ``variable``, ``label``, ``unit``, ``years``, ``scale``, ``units`` (with data) and ``description``. Pass the ``dataset`` and ``variable`` to ``geo.load(dataset, variables=variable)``. |\n\n## Example {.doc-section .doc-section-example}\n\n```python\n!pip install -q geo4bolivia\nimport geo4bolivia as geo\nimport plotly.express as px\n\nhits = geo.search(\"education women\")       # every word must match\ndisplay(hits[[\"dataset\", \"variable\", \"label\", \"years\"]])\ndf = geo.load(hits[\"dataset\"][0], variables=hits[\"variable\"][0], names=True)\npx.box(df, x=\"year\", y=hits[\"variable\"][0], hover_name=\"name\",\n       labels=geo.labels(df), title=hits[\"label\"][0])\n```\n\n\n::: {#5c6c4063 .cell execution_count=1}\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display}\n```{=html}\n<div>\n<style scoped>\n    .dataframe tbody tr th:only-of-type {\n        vertical-align: middle;\n    }\n\n    .dataframe tbody tr th {\n        vertical-align: top;\n    }\n\n    .dataframe thead th {\n        text-align: right;\n    }\n</style>\n<table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\">\n  <thead>\n    <tr style=\"text-align: right;\">\n      <th></th>\n      <th>dataset</th>\n      <th>variable</th>\n      <th>label</th>\n      <th>years</th>\n    </tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr>\n      <th>0</th>\n      <td>sdg04</td>\n      <td>sdg4_3_aem</td>\n      <td>Years of education, women 25-35</td>\n      <td>2012, 2024</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>1</th>\n      <td>sdg04</td>\n      <td>sdg4_3_esm</td>\n      <td>Higher education, women 19+ (%)</td>\n      <td>2012, 2024</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>2</th>\n      <td>sdg05</td>\n      <td>sdg5_1_pge</td>\n      <td>Gender parity in years of education, 25-35 (wo...</td>\n      <td>2012, 2024</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>3</th>\n      <td>sdg08</td>\n      <td>sdg8_6_etm</td>\n      <td>Young women not in education or the labour for...</td>\n      <td>2012, 2024</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>4</th>\n      <td>sdg04</td>\n      <td>index_sdg4</td>\n      <td>Quality education index (0-100)</td>\n      <td>2012, 2024</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>5</th>\n      <td>sdg05</td>\n      <td>index_sdg5</td>\n      <td>Gender equality index (0-100)</td>\n      <td>2012, 2024</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>6</th>\n      <td>sdg08</td>\n      <td>index_sdg8</td>\n      <td>Decent work and economic growth index (0-100)</td>\n      <td>2012, 2024</td>\n    </tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n</div>\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display}\n